+# Gate
+
+- **Mandatory class**: none
+- **Depth**: standard (the class is none and no review, gate or release mechanism changes)
+- **Risk tier**: product
+- **Author's risk assessment**: The change rewrites the dashboard's in-memory render cache and adds one runtime dependency. Worst realistic failures: wrong recency order evicting hot widgets (extra renders, slower refresh), a stale-props bug left in place (a widget showing outdated data until reload), or an accounting error letting memory grow past the budget. No persistence, credentials, user data or network boundary is involved, and every failure is recovered by a page reload. `src/cache.ts` is an exported module of a private, unpublished package whose signatures stay unchanged, so no independently released contract exists (class `none`); it ships in the product dashboard, so the tier is `product`.
+- **Whole-diff review**: not needed (whole-diff surface reviewed in F2)
+- **Accepted residual risks**: Props changes confined to function-, `undefined`- or symbol-valued keys are invisible to the JSON fingerprint, so such a widget is served its previous HTML until `invalidate(id)`; the props fingerprint is held in memory but not counted against the byte budget, so actual memory can exceed the budget by the size of the cached widgets' serialized props.
+- **Out of scope for blocking**: Escaping `w.id` in `src/render.ts` (separate roadmap follow-up, file untouched by this change); time-based expiry of entries; any code in the dashboard shell outside this repository.
