+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+The render cache in `src/cache.ts` grows without bound: every widget rendered stays in memory until `invalidate` or `clear`, so a long-running dashboard holds the HTML of every widget it ever showed. The widget roadmap (`docs/roadmap/widgets.md`, Next) schedules size-based eviction for the render cache, and the cache also serves stale HTML when a widget's props change, which a bounded cache would keep doing.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- The render cache gets a byte budget: the accounted size of the cache is the UTF-8 byte length of the HTML it holds, and it never exceeds the budget after a render. Default budget 1 MiB (1,048,576 bytes); the dashboard can change it at runtime.
+- When storing a new render would exceed the budget, the least recently used entries are evicted until it fits. Serving a widget from the cache and reading its HTML by id count as use; checking presence does not.
+- Rendered HTML larger than the whole budget is returned to the caller but not stored; a previous entry for that widget is dropped so it cannot be served stale.
+- Lowering the budget evicts least recently used entries immediately; a budget that is not a positive integer is rejected and the budget stays unchanged.
+- The cache reports its accounted byte total next to the existing entry count.
+- A render of a widget whose props differ from the props its cached HTML was rendered with re-renders and replaces the entry instead of returning the old HTML (follow-up below). Props that cannot be serialized to JSON bypass the cache.
+- `get`, `has`, `invalidate`, `clear`, `size` and `render` keep their signatures. Behaviour change for callers: an entry can now disappear without `invalidate`/`clear`, which `get`'s existing `string | undefined` return already allows.
+- New runtime dependency `lru-cache` (see design.md, Build vs. adopt).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `widget-render-cache`: the dashboard's cache of rendered widget HTML — when it serves cached HTML, when it re-renders, and how its memory is bounded.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None (the project has no specs yet; the earlier `widget-cache` change declared `skip_specs`).
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/cache.ts`: storage moves to a size-bounded LRU; new budget setter and byte-total accessor; props check in `render`.
+- `src/render.ts`, `src/widget.ts`: unchanged.
+- `package.json`: adds `lru-cache` as a dependency and a `test` script; adds `bun.lock`.
+- New tests under `test/` (the repository has none today), run with `bun test`.
+- Dashboard shell (not in this repository): may call the new budget setter; nothing it calls today changes signature.
+
+## Follow-ups taken
+
+- `docs/roadmap/widgets.md`: `get` keys entries by widget id only, so a widget whose props changed still renders its old HTML. `src/cache.ts:12`. Source: `widget-shell` .omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-shell/f2/trailer-strategic-risk-review.txt, B1
