+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Keeps the rendered HTML of dashboard widgets so unchanged widgets are not re-rendered on every refresh, while bounding the memory the cache holds.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Byte budget bounds the cache
+The render cache SHALL keep the accounted size of its entries at or below its byte budget after every operation. An entry's accounted size is the UTF-8 byte length of its rendered HTML. The default budget is 1,048,576 bytes.
+
+#### Scenario: Renders beyond the budget stay within it
+- **WHEN** the budget is 100 bytes and widgets whose HTML is 40 bytes each are rendered one after another, five in total
+- **THEN** after each render the cache's reported byte total is at most 100 and it holds at most two entries
+
+#### Scenario: Default budget
+- **WHEN** the cache is used without setting a budget
+- **THEN** cached HTML totalling exactly 1,048,576 bytes is held in full, and rendering one more widget evicts the least recently used entry
+
+#### Scenario: Negative control
+- **WHEN** the budget is 100 bytes and a third 40-byte widget is rendered while two 40-byte entries are cached
+- **THEN** a cache that then reports a byte total of 120 or holds three entries MUST fail the check
+
+### Requirement: Least recently used entries are evicted first
+When storing a render would exceed the budget, the cache SHALL evict entries in least-recently-used order until the new entry fits, and SHALL keep the new entry. Storing an entry, serving a widget's HTML from the cache, and reading an entry's HTML by widget id mark it most recently used; checking whether an entry exists does not.
+
+#### Scenario: A served entry survives eviction
+- **WHEN** the budget holds two 40-byte entries, widgets A then B are rendered, A is rendered again and served from the cache, then widget C is rendered
+- **THEN** B is evicted and A and C remain cached
+
+#### Scenario: Reading by id counts as use
+- **WHEN** widgets A then B are cached at a budget of two entries, A's HTML is read by id, then widget C is rendered
+- **THEN** B is evicted and A remains cached
+
+#### Scenario: Presence check does not count as use
+- **WHEN** widgets A then B are cached at a budget of two entries, the cache is asked whether A exists, then widget C is rendered
+- **THEN** A is evicted and B remains cached
+
+#### Scenario: Negative control
+- **WHEN** A then B are cached at a budget of two entries, A is served from the cache, then C is rendered
+- **THEN** a cache that evicts A (insertion order instead of use order) MUST fail the check
+
+### Requirement: Output larger than the budget is not cached
+When a widget's rendered HTML is larger than the whole budget, the cache SHALL return that HTML to the caller without storing it, SHALL drop any entry it held for that widget, and SHALL leave every other entry in place.
+
+#### Scenario: Oversized render is returned but not stored
+- **WHEN** the budget is 100 bytes, widget B is cached, and widget A renders 150 bytes of HTML
+- **THEN** the render returns A's 150-byte HTML, A is not cached, and B is still cached
+
+#### Scenario: Oversized re-render drops the old entry
+- **WHEN** widget A is cached with 40 bytes of HTML and its props change so that it now renders 150 bytes at a budget of 100
+- **THEN** A is no longer cached and reading A's HTML by id returns nothing
+
+#### Scenario: Negative control
+- **WHEN** the budget is 100 bytes and widget A renders 150 bytes of HTML while B is cached
+- **THEN** a cache that evicts B, stores A, or keeps A's earlier HTML MUST fail the check
+
+### Requirement: Budget can be changed at runtime
+The cache SHALL accept a new byte budget that is a positive integer. Lowering the budget SHALL evict least recently used entries immediately until the cache fits. A budget that is zero, negative, fractional or not a finite number SHALL be rejected with an error, leaving the budget and every entry unchanged.
+
+#### Scenario: Lowering the budget evicts at once
+- **WHEN** widgets A, B and C (40 bytes each) are cached in that order at the default budget and the budget is set to 80 bytes
+- **THEN** A is evicted before any further render, and B and C remain cached
+
+#### Scenario: Raising the budget keeps entries
+- **WHEN** two 40-byte entries are cached at a budget of 80 bytes and the budget is raised to 200
+- **THEN** both entries remain cached and a third 40-byte render evicts nothing
+
+#### Scenario: Negative control
+- **WHEN** the budget is set to 0, -1, 1.5 or NaN while entries are cached
+- **THEN** a cache that accepts the value, changes its budget, or evicts any entry MUST fail the check
+
+### Requirement: Cache reports its accounted bytes
+The cache SHALL report its current byte total, equal to the sum of the accounted sizes of the entries it holds, alongside the existing entry count. Removing one entry or clearing the cache SHALL reduce the total by the removed entries' sizes.
+
+#### Scenario: Total follows stores and removals
+- **WHEN** widgets with 40 and 30 bytes of HTML are cached, then the first is invalidated, then the cache is cleared
+- **THEN** the reported total is 70, then 30, then 0, and the entry count is 2, then 1, then 0
+
+#### Scenario: Multi-byte characters count as bytes
+- **WHEN** a widget whose HTML contains the character "€" (3 bytes in UTF-8) is cached
+- **THEN** the reported total counts that character as 3 bytes, not 1
+
+#### Scenario: Negative control
+- **WHEN** a widget's HTML contains "€" and is cached
+- **THEN** a cache that reports the HTML's UTF-16 length instead of its UTF-8 byte length MUST fail the check
+
+### Requirement: Changed props are re-rendered
+When a widget is rendered and the cache holds HTML for its id that was rendered from props whose JSON serialization differs from the widget's current props, the cache SHALL render the widget again, return the new HTML, and replace the cached entry with it.
+
+#### Scenario: Props change produces new HTML
+- **WHEN** widget A is rendered with props `{"title":"Sales"}`, its props change to `{"title":"Costs"}`, and A is rendered again
+- **THEN** the second render returns HTML produced from `{"title":"Costs"}` and that HTML is what the cache now holds for A
+
+#### Scenario: Unchanged props are served from the cache
+- **WHEN** widget A is rendered twice with props `{"title":"Sales"}` and nothing in between
+- **THEN** the widget's own render runs once and the second call returns the cached HTML
+
+#### Scenario: Negative control
+- **WHEN** widget A is rendered with props `{"title":"Sales"}`, its props change to `{"title":"Costs"}`, and A is rendered again
+- **THEN** a cache that returns the HTML rendered from `{"title":"Sales"}` MUST fail the check
+
+### Requirement: Props that cannot be serialized bypass the cache
+When a widget's props cannot be serialized to JSON (for example they contain a cycle or a BigInt), the cache SHALL render the widget on every call, return the fresh HTML, store nothing for it, and drop any entry it held for that widget id.
+
+#### Scenario: Cyclic props render fresh each time
+- **WHEN** widget A has props that reference themselves and is rendered twice
+- **THEN** the widget's own render runs twice, both calls return its HTML, and A is not cached
+
+#### Scenario: Negative control
+- **WHEN** widget A was cached with serializable props and is then rendered with props containing a BigInt
+- **THEN** a cache that throws, returns A's earlier HTML, or still holds an entry for A MUST fail the check
