+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Dependency and test runner
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Add `lru-cache` pinned to `11.5.3` (`bun add --exact lru-cache@11.5.3`, which writes `bun.lock`) and a `"test": "bun test"` script to `package.json`. Verify: `bun install --frozen-lockfile && jq -e '.dependencies["lru-cache"] == "11.5.3" and .scripts.test == "bun test"' package.json && bun -e "import { LRUCache } from 'lru-cache'; if (typeof LRUCache !== 'function') process.exit(1)"`
+
+## 2. Size-bounded LRU storage
+
+- [ ] 2.1 In `src/cache.ts`, replace the `Map` with an `LRUCache` keyed by widget id holding `CacheEntry` values, per design D1/D2: export `DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES = 1_048_576`, `totalBytes()` and `setMaxBytes(bytes)` (RangeError for non-safe-integer or ≤ 0 before any state change; rebuild from `rentries()` to keep recency); `sizeCalculation` is the UTF-8 byte length from a module-level `TextEncoder`; `get`, `has`, `invalidate`, `clear`, `size` keep their signatures. Update the file's header comment to describe the byte-bounded LRU. Add `test/cache.test.ts` (`bun:test`, `beforeEach` → `clear()` + `setMaxBytes(DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES)`, a helper that builds a widget with an exact rendered byte length and counts its `render()` calls) with `describe` blocks named "Byte budget bounds the cache", "Cache reports its accounted bytes" and "Budget can be changed at runtime", covering every scenario of those three requirements, the negative controls included (five 40-byte renders at 100 never exceed 100 bytes/2 entries; exact 1,048,576 bytes held at the default and one more render evicts; "€" counts 3; 0, -1, 1.5 and NaN throw and leave budget and entries unchanged). Verify: `bun test test/cache.test.ts -t "Byte budget bounds the cache|Cache reports its accounted bytes|Budget can be changed at runtime"`
+- [ ] 2.2 Add `describe` blocks "Least recently used entries are evicted first" (render hit and `get` keep A, `has` does not; insertion-order eviction must fail) and "Output larger than the budget is not cached" with its first scenario and negative control for a new widget (150 bytes at budget 100 is returned, not stored, B kept). Fix `src/cache.ts` if any case fails (for example a `maxEntrySize` override or a recency-touching `has`). Verify: `bun test test/cache.test.ts -t "Least recently used entries are evicted first|Output larger than the budget is not cached"`
+- [ ] 2.3 Remove the delivered `- Size-based eviction for the render cache.` bullet from `## Next` in `docs/roadmap/widgets.md`, leaving `## Follow-ups` untouched. Verify: `! grep -qxF -- '- Size-based eviction for the render cache.' docs/roadmap/widgets.md && grep -qxF -- '- Keyboard navigation between widgets.' docs/roadmap/widgets.md && test "$(grep -c '^- ' docs/roadmap/widgets.md)" = 3`
+
+## 3. Props-aware rendering (taken follow-up)
+
+- [ ] 3.1 In `render(widget)`, add `propsKey` (the `JSON.stringify(widget.props)` the HTML was rendered from) to `CacheEntry` and serve a hit only when it equals the current fingerprint; otherwise re-render and replace the entry under the same id (design D3). Add `describe` "Changed props are re-rendered" (Sales → Costs returns new HTML and the cache holds it; unchanged props render once; returning Sales HTML must fail) and, inside "Output larger than the budget is not cached", the scenario "Oversized re-render drops the old entry" (40-byte A whose props change to a 150-byte render at budget 100 is no longer cached and `get("A")` is `undefined`). Verify: `bun test test/cache.test.ts -t "Changed props are re-rendered|Oversized re-render drops the old entry"`
+- [ ] 3.2 When the fingerprint throws or is `undefined`, delete any entry for the id and return `renderWidget(widget)` without storing. Add `describe` "Props that cannot be serialized bypass the cache" (cyclic props render twice and are not cached; A cached with serializable props then rendered with a BigInt prop does not throw, returns fresh HTML and leaves no entry). Verify: `bun test test/cache.test.ts -t "Props that cannot be serialized bypass the cache" && bun test`
+
+## 4. Final verification
+
+- [ ] 4.1 F1. Manual QA on the real surface: merge the default branch (`main`) into the work branch when it is not an ancestor of the head, and commit; then, on the head after the last code commit, drive the real `src/cache.ts` (with the real `src/render.ts` and `lru-cache`) from a `bun` QA script and capture its printed output for each row: row-01 byte budget (five 40-byte renders at budget 100: `totalBytes()`/`size()` after each never above 100/2); row-02 LRU order (A, B, A served, C → keys B evicted; `get` variant keeps A; `has` variant evicts A); row-03 oversized output (150-byte new widget returned, not stored, B kept; 40-byte A re-rendered at 150 bytes leaves no entry); row-04 runtime budget (A, B, C then 80 → A evicted at once; raise to 200 keeps both; 0, -1, 1.5, NaN throw RangeError with budget and entries unchanged); row-05 accounted bytes (70 → 30 → 0 with counts 2 → 1 → 0; "€" HTML counted as 3 bytes); row-06 changed props (Sales → Costs returns Costs HTML, render count 2; unchanged props render count 1); row-07 unserializable props (cyclic props render twice, no entry; BigInt after a cached render returns fresh HTML, no entry, no throw); row-08 happy path (40 widgets with realistic props rendered twice at the default budget: second pass is 40 hits and 0 renders; time per hit vs per render printed); row-09 riskiest edge (an entry of exactly the budget is cached, budget + 1 is not; exactly 1,048,576 bytes held at the default and the next render evicts the least recently used entry); row-10 regression (in-budget `get`/`has`/`invalidate`/`clear`/`size` behave as before and `git diff --exit-code main -- src/render.ts src/widget.ts` is empty). One evidence path per row in `.omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-cache-size-eviction/f1/`: `row-01-byte-budget.txt`, `row-02-lru-order.txt`, `row-03-oversized.txt`, `row-04-runtime-budget.txt`, `row-05-accounted-bytes.txt`, `row-06-changed-props.txt`, `row-07-unserializable-props.txt`, `row-08-happy-path.txt`, `row-09-budget-edge.txt`, `row-10-regression.txt`; the QA lane judges the observations. Verify: `d=.omp/team-config/evidence/gate/widget-cache-size-eviction/f1; for f in row-01-byte-budget row-02-lru-order row-03-oversized row-04-runtime-budget row-05-accounted-bytes row-06-changed-props row-07-unserializable-props row-08-happy-path row-09-budget-edge row-10-regression; do test -s "$d/$f.txt" || { echo "missing $f"; exit 1; }; done`
+
